{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Therefore say</b> Two times in the Masorah: לכן אמר לבני ישראל — לכן אמר הנני נותן לו את בריתי שלום. As expounded in the Sifrei: Everything Moses did, Phinehas did. Moses was sent as emissary to bring Israel out of Egypt, and Phinehas will be emissary to bring Israel out of exile, and likewise all the deeds Moses did, Phinehas also did. Therefore עולה ק — in the merit of Abraham, who begot a son at one hundred, and Isaac, who found a hundred gates, and Jacob, who begot all his offspring at one hundred years, they went out." "<b>And I will bring out, and I will deliver, and I will redeem, and I will take</b> Four expressions of redemption, corresponding to four kingdoms. And in the last one it is written ולקחתי, corresponding to Edom; therefore it is written with it ולקחתי — like a man who takes by force, which is harder than all of them. והוצאתי והצלתי וגאלתי ולקחתי in gematria — this teaches that a poor man in Israel must not be given less than four cups."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:12:16.136707091Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}